            %a{:href => "#BousfieldGugenheim76"}> Bousfield-Gugenheim 76, Theorems 9.4 &amp; 11.2
            )
          %h3#preservation_of_homotopy_pullbacks Preservation of homotopy pullbacks
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              The left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+functor"} Quillen left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo :
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi dgAlg
                      %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet : sSet \to dgAlg_{\mathbb{Q}}
              preserves
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullbacks"} homotopy pullbacks
              of objects of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
              (each rational homotopy group is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+space"} finite dimensional vector space
              over the
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            %p
              In other words in the induced pair of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} adjoint (∞,1)-functors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi dgAlg
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mi op
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\Omega^\bullet \dashv K)
                    \:
                    (dgAlg_\mathbb{Q}^{op})^\circ
                    \\stackrel{\overset{}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{}{\to}}
                    \\infty Grpd
            %p
              the left adjoint preserves
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+in+a+quasi-category"} (∞,1)-categorical pullbacks
              of objects of finite type.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              This is effectively a restatement of a result that appears below proposition 15.8 in HalperinThomas and is reproduced in some repackaged form as theorem 2.2 of
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uic.edu/~bshipley/hess_ratlhtpy.pdf"} He06
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category-theoretic
              context that allows to rephrase this result in the above form.
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                    %mo ←
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = \{a \to c \leftarrow b\}
              be the pullback
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              category.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
              functor is the right
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} lim_C
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              (described in detail at
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+Kan+extension"} homotopy Kan extension
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi inj
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ⊥
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi lim
                            %mi C
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi const
                    %mi sSet
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [C,sSet]_{inj}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{lim_C}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{const}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\;\;\; \bot \;\;\;}
                    sSet
                    \\,.
            %p
              At
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+functors"} model structure on functors
              it is discussed that composition with the Quillen pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet \dashv K
              induces a Quillen adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi dgAlg
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ⊥
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi C
                          %mo ,
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi C
                          %mo ,
                          %msup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ([C,\Omega^\bullet] \dashv [C,K])
                    \\;\colon\;
                    [C, dgAlg^{op}]
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{[C,K]}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{[C,\Omega^\bullet]}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\;\; \bot \;\;}
                    [C,sSet]
                    \\,.
            %p
              We need to show that for every fibrant and cofibrant pullback diagram
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \in [C,sSet]
              there exists a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mi C
                    %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mi C
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ^
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega^\bullet \circ lim_C F
                    \\;\;
                    \\simeq
                    \\;\;
                    lim_C   \widehat{\Omega^\bullet(F)}
                    \\,,
            %p
              here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{\Omega^\bullet(F)}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+replacement"} fibrant replacement
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(F)
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi dgAlg
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgAlg^{op}
            %p
              Now, every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi inj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in [C,sSet]_{inj}
              is cofibrant, and it is fibrant if all three objects
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(a)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(b)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(c)
              are fibrant and one of the two morphisms is a fibration. We may assume without restriction of generality that it is the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(a) \to F(c)
              that is a fibration. So we assume that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(a), F(b)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(c)
              are three
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
              and that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(a) \to F(b)
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} lim_C
              sends
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              to the ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mi C
                    %mi F
                    %mo =
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} lim_C F = F(a) \times_{F(c)} F(b)
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega^\bullet(F(a) \times_{F(c)} F(b))
                    \\,.
            %p
              Recall that the
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+algebra"} Sullivan algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi dgAlg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgAlg
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi dgAlg
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgAlg^{op}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(F)
              may be obtained by
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  first choosing a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+model"} Sullivan model
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mo ∧
                          %mo •
                        %mi V
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mo ≃
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\wedge^\bullet V, d_V) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \Omega^\bullet(c)
              %li
                %p
                  then choosing factorizations in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi dgAlg
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgAlg
                  of the composites of this with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(F(c)) \to \Omega^\bullet(F(a))
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(F(c)) \to \Omega^\bullet(F(b))
                  into cofibrations follows by weak equivalences.
            %p The result is a diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mo ∧
                              %mo •
                            %msup
                              %mi U
                              %mo *
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mo ∧
                              %mo •
                            %msup
                              %mi V
                              %mo *
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mi V
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mo ∧
                              %mo •
                            %msup
                              %mi W
                              %mo *
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mi W
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mo ≃
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ←
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    (\wedge^\bullet U^*, d_U)
                    \&amp;\leftarrow&amp;
                    (\wedge^\bullet V^*, d_V)
                    \&amp;\hookrightarrow&amp;
                    (\wedge^\bullet W^* , d_W)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\simeq}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\simeq}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\simeq}
                    \\\
                    \\Omega^\bullet(F(a))
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\leftarrow}&amp;
                    \\Omega^\bullet(F(c))
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp;
                    \\Omega^\bullet(F(b))
                    }
            %p
              that in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi dgAlg
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgAlg^{op}
              exhibits a fibrant replacement of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(F)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi dgAlg
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgAlg^{op}
              is the colimit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mo ∧
                          %mo •
                        %msup
                          %mi V
                          %mo *
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\wedge^\bullet U^* , d_U)
                    \\otimes_{(\wedge^\bullet V^* , d_V)}
                    (\wedge^\bullet W^* , d_W)
            %p
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi dgAlg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgAlg
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mo ∧
                          %mo •
                        %msup
                          %mi V
                          %mo *
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\wedge^\bullet U^* , d_U)
                    \\otimes_{(\wedge^\bullet V^* , d_V)}
                    (\wedge^\bullet W^* , d_W)
                    \\simeq
                    \\Omega^\bullet(F(a) \times_{F(c)} F(b))
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is precisely the statement of that quoted result
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uic.edu/~bshipley/hess_ratlhtpy.pdf"} He, theorem 2.2
          %blockquote
            %p check the following
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p Rationalization preserves homotopy pullbacks of objects of finite type.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              The theory of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+model"} Sullivan model
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (a simplicial set
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo •
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Omega^\bullet \dashv K)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              applied to a Sullivan model
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\wedge^\bullet V^*, d)
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(X)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi K
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi K
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ^
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \to K \Omega^\bullet(X) \stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow} K \widehat {\Omega^\bullet(X)} := K (\wedge^\bullet V^* , d_V)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Being a Quillen right adjoint, the right derived functor of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              of course preserves homotopy limits. Hence the composite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ∘
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \circ \widehat{\Omega^\bullet(-)}
              preserves homotopy pullbacks between objects of finite type.
          %h3#preservation_of_homotopy_fibers Preservation of homotopy fibers
          %p
